  "reconstructionNotes": "Center the horizontal optical axis in the canvas. The lens is a tall, pale blue oval. Draw the object as a solid red arrow pointing up. Ensure the three rays originate exactly from the object's tip, bend exactly at the vertical center line of the lens, and intersect precisely at the tip of the inverted image arrow. Ray 1 is red, Ray 2 is green, Ray 3 is purple. Distance brackets (d_o, d_i) sit neatly below the axis. Ensure mathematical labels (h_o, h_i, d_o, d_i, f) use an italic serif font with proper subscripts."
